      "eventMetadata": {
        "context_description": "Recent high-level boundary talks in Beijing on August 25-26, 2026, between China’s Foreign Minister Wang Yi and India’s National Security Adviser Ajit Doval produced an eight-point consensus that includes new military hotlines, additional commander-level meeting points, and working groups to advance delimitation of less contentious border sections. Both sides reaffirmed commitments to peace and tranquility along the Line of Actual Control, prompt use of existing diplomatic and military channels to address incidents, and scheduled expert talks on trans-border rivers for September. These steps build on the 2024 disengagement agreement and prior leader-level engagements, following reports of localized patrol frictions in Arunachal Pradesh earlier in August that Indian officials largely downplayed. The upcoming BRICS summit in New Delhi later in September offers further opportunity for sustained dialogue, while the next formal boundary round is set for India in 2027.",
