        "context_description": "NATO and EU member states continue channeling extensive military aid, training, and equipment to Ukraine through mechanisms such as the NATO Security Assistance and Training for Ukraine command and EU missions, while maintaining multinational battlegroups strictly on alliance territory along the eastern flank. A UK- and France-led Coalition of the Willing has advanced plans since early 2026 for a multinational force to deploy only after a credible ceasefire, focused on deterrence, training, and security guarantees rather than direct combat roles. Recent developments include coalition meetings in August 2026 to refine post-hostilities arrangements, joint drills scheduled in Poland for October-November, and repeated Russian statements rejecting any NATO contingents. No official commitments or deployments for combat operations inside Ukraine have occurred, with support remaining calibrated to avoid escalation and aligned with ongoing diplomatic efforts toward de-escalation.",
