      "estimateValue": false,
      "eventMetadata": {
        "context_description": "Ongoing martial law, extended through October 31, 2026, and Ukraine’s constitution and election law explicitly prohibit presidential or parliamentary votes while it remains in effect, forming the central barrier to any early call. Recent public calls by former Defense Minister Mykhailo Fedorov for wartime elections prompted sharp pushback from President Zelenskyy, who described the process as too risky amid active Russian strikes and potential internal divisions. Polling shows most Ukrainians favor waiting until after a ceasefire or peace agreement with security guarantees. Preparations would require new legislation, updated voter rolls for millions displaced or serving in the military, and months of logistical setup. No national election date has been announced, and cross-party consensus ties any vote to the lifting of martial law plus a six-month preparation window.",
